+## D11 — Native rectangle-scope family (review-2897d39f7102ccb7)
+
+**Decision:** preserve the exact canonical `all_rectangles` Racket program and add `largest_interior`, which parses the one-gap rectangles, computes each interior area, selects the unique largest interior, and applies the canonical fill-and-ray transform only to that rectangle.
+
+**Why this parameter:** the source rule's geometric parser and gap-direction logic remain intact. The variant introduces a meaningful input-derived selector whose exact rectangle identity controls both the filled interior and projected ray.
+
+**Teaching contract:** the minimum two demonstrations deliberately distinguish largest interior area from largest outline size and alternate source order. Declared smallest/first/last/largest-outline/no-ray/no-fill rivals are rejected before the four private queries; inputs are matched across settings and count prefixes are stable.
