+# Parametric rectangle scope
+
+`all_rectangles` preserves the exact canonical rule: fill every one-gap
+rectangle and extend a red ray from each gap to the canvas edge.
+`largest_interior` computes each rectangle's interior area, selects the unique
+largest rectangle, and applies the same fill-and-ray operation only to that
+input-derived object.
+
+The first two demonstrations deliberately alternate whether the selected object
+is first or last in reading order. The first also separates interior area from
+outline perimeter (6×6 versus 3×10). Episodes support 2–6 demonstrations and
+stable 1–4 query prefixes. The fourth query is a 30×30 four-rectangle stress case
+with boundary contacts and 110 outline cells.
